# The repo is edited on Windows and executed on Linux. Anything the container
# runs must keep LF endings — a CRLF shebang makes the kernel look for an
# interpreter literally named "/bin/sh\r", and the error says "no such file or
# directory" while pointing at a file that plainly exists.
*.sh            text eol=lf
Dockerfile      text eol=lf
*.yml           text eol=lf
*.yaml          text eol=lf
entrypoint.sh   text eol=lf
